abstract: >-
  Agentpower (AP) is a unit of cognitive work output. One AP is the
  quality-adjusted output of one full-time-equivalent year of knowledge work
  in a given role, at that role's productivity without generative AI.
  Specification 2.0 defines two standard measures, realised AP (AP-Q:
  audited output per FTE against a control group) and capacity AP (AP-C: a
  task-based Amdahl bound), recalibrates the stage bands to the 2023-2026
  evidence, and replaces the token-based cost method with a cost per measured
  AP gain. The choice of methods is supported by a reproducible Monte Carlo
  study included in the repository.
